{*
	Constructs that exist only in the Latte 3 line. A project on 2.11 - which is
	what the playground's composer.json declares - would fail to compile this
	file, and that is the point of keeping it separate: mixing these into the
	general templates would make every proklik show something red and the red
	would stop meaning anything.

	Nothing here may be underlined either. The plugin has no version switch yet
	(see .ai/plans/05-detekce-verze-latte.md), so it accepts the union of the
	supported range - which is the direction that cannot produce a false error.
	When the switch lands, this file is its first real test: with the project set
	to 2.11 these lines should light up, and with it set to 3.x they must not.

	Where each item came in:
	  {exitIf} 3.0.5 | n:else 3.0.12 | n:elseif 3.1.0 | {syntax single} 3.0.24
	  filters: escape 3.0.5, group 3.0.16, localDate 3.0.18, filter 3.0.20,
	           firstLower 3.0.22, column/commas/limit 3.1.3, map 3.1.6
	  functions: hasBlock 3.0.10, group 3.0.16, hasTemplate 3.0.22
*}
{var $items = [['id' => 1, 'group' => 'a'], ['id' => 2, 'group' => 'b']]}
{var $text = 'Some Text'}
{var $when = '2026-01-31'}
{var $show = false}

{exitIf !$items}

<p n:if="$show">The condition held.</p>
<p n:else>And this is what runs when it did not.</p>

<p n:if="$show">First branch.</p>
<p n:elseif="$items">Second branch.</p>
<p n:else>Third branch.</p>

{* Filters added inside the 3.x line *}
{$text|escape}
{$text|firstLower}
{$items|column:'id'|implode:', '}
{$items|column:'id'|commas}
{$items|limit:1|column:'id'|implode:', '}
{$items|map:fn($item) => $item['id']|implode:', '}
{$items|filter:fn($item) => $item['id'] > 1|column:'id'|implode:', '}
{$when|localDate:'medium'}
{foreach ($items|group:'group') as $key => $group}
	<p>{$key}: {$group|column:'id'|implode:', '}</p>
{/foreach}

{* Functions added inside the 3.x line *}
{foreach group($items, 'group') as $key => $group}
	<p>{$key}: {$group|column:'id'|implode:', '}</p>
{/foreach}
<p n:if="hasBlock('content')">The block exists.</p>
<p n:if="hasTemplate('inheritance-card.latte')">The template exists.</p>

{* Directives Latte 3.1 recognises in an HTML attribute value, and the one
   camelCase spelling of |nocheck that Latte 3 accepts. *}
<div data-open="{$show|toggle}">toggle</div>
<div data-payload="{$items|json}">json</div>
<div data-id="{$items|accept:'number'}">accept</div>
<a href="{$text|noCheck}">noCheck</a>

{* nette/assets, a Latte 3 package: it has no Latte 2 bridge at all. *}
<img src="{asset 'images/logo.png'}" alt="">
<img n:asset="'images/logo.png'" alt="">
<img n:asset?="'images/optional.png'" alt="">
{preload 'images/logo.png'}
<p>{asset('images/logo.png')->url}</p>
<p n:if="tryAsset('images/optional.png')">The asset exists.</p>

{* Single-brace mode, spelled out from 3.0.24 on. Closing it is optional, as
   with every other {syntax} mode. *}
{syntax single}
{$text}
